* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
* ok = !READCSVROW(f, delim, quote, esc, row)
*
* Reads the next line of the sequential file F into ROW.  A CSV field that is enclosed in quotes may hold a line break, so when the
* line ends inside an enclosed field (CSVOPEN) the next line is read as well and joined on with a line feed, and so on until the
* field is closed or the file ends.  DELIM, QUOTE and ESC are the characters of the dialect; a null string is a comma, a double
* quote and no escape character.  Gives 1 when a row was read and 0 at the end of the file (ROW is a null string).  A file that
* ends inside an enclosed field gives the row as far as it went.
*
* READCSV has never taken its rules from CSV.MODE; it still does not.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
function readcsvrow(f, delim, quote, esc, row)
$catalog !readcsvrow

   readseq row from f else
      row = ''
      return 0
   end

   loop
   while csvopen(row, delim, quote, esc)
      readseq more from f else exit
      row := char(10) : more
   repeat

   return 1
end

* END-CODE
